Once I was preaching this sermon, I kind of like using this as an example because part of the problem that we have in the world is that we don't fully understand that God,

321
00:43:57,540 --> 00:44:01,540
it's not only that he loves us, but that he's always loved us.

322
00:44:01,540 --> 00:44:04,540
There's no need to earn God's love.

323
00:44:04,540 --> 00:44:08,540
Listen, this might sound like a controversial thing.

324
00:44:08,540 --> 00:44:13,540
God didn't start loving you when Jesus died for your sins.

325
00:44:13,540 --> 00:44:19,540
God didn't start loving you when you repented and received salvation.

326
00:44:19,540 --> 00:44:23,540
God loved you before. Jesus said, "For God so loved the world that he gave his son."

327
00:44:23,540 --> 00:44:26,540
God loved you so that he sent his son.

328
00:44:26,540 --> 00:44:30,540
God loved you so he died for you.

329
00:44:30,540 --> 00:44:34,540
When Jesus died on the cross, what is he saying?

330
00:44:34,540 --> 00:44:38,540
I love you.

331
00:44:38,540 --> 00:44:43,540
I have always loved you.

332
00:44:43,540 --> 00:44:47,540
You know one of the reasons why we have church every Sunday?

333
00:44:47,540 --> 00:44:52,540
It's not only so we can do this event and people can come and hear about Jesus, which is important.

334
00:44:52,540 --> 00:44:56,540
It's only so we can sing songs and learn more.

335
00:44:56,540 --> 00:45:00,540
It's because we forget.

336
00:45:00,540 --> 00:45:07,540
When the problems of life happen, when the conflicts of life happen, when we don't remain in God and don't spend time praying in the Word,

337
00:45:07,540 --> 00:45:18,540
it's so easy to forget that God loves us, that God has always loved us.

338
00:45:18,540 --> 00:45:28,540
So week after week, we gather together in a room, and we sing songs about the love of Jesus.

339
00:45:28,540 --> 00:45:40,540
And week after week, we are about to take communion, we take a piece of bread and we take a piece of wine to tell ourselves God loves us.

340
00:45:40,540 --> 00:45:57,540
God has always loved us. And if you hear anything today, it's that. And as you open yourself to that love, you know what hasn't happened?

341
00:45:57,540 --> 00:46:10,540
That love is going to become a fruit in your life. Let's pray. God, words fail me to talk about your love.

342
00:46:10,540 --> 00:46:20,540
There's not enough ink. There's not enough. We have to basically reinvent the word to even begin to comprehend your love.

343
00:46:20,540 --> 00:46:34,540
And God, my prayer is that this morning, as we gather around the bread and the wine, that your spirit is the only one that can give us a full revelation of your love.

344
00:46:34,540 --> 00:46:51,540
We awaken something in our hearts. We open our eyes to the love that you have for us. We believe that you love us. You have always loved us. In the name of Jesus we pray. Amen.
